    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Behind the technical name InstructGPT, what intuitive problem were researchers confronting?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Large pretrained models could complete text fluently but did not reliably infer a user's intent. InstructGPT emerged from earlier human-preference research as a direct attempt to align model behavior after pretraining.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-instructgpt-paper", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "The pipeline first fine-tunes on human demonstrations, then learns a reward model from ranked responses, and finally optimizes the policy with PPO. Keeping these stages separate turns qualitative preference judgments into a trainable signal.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-instructgpt-paper", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Why did the idea outlive one paper or experiment? What did later researchers actually inherit?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Experts generally treat InstructGPT as the operational template for modern RLHF post-training. Its importance lies less in raw parameter scale than in showing that smaller aligned models can be preferred over much larger untuned baselines.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-instructgpt-paper", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "SUMMARY",
            "text": "InstructGPT mattered not only as a result, but as a method that later researchers could test, adapt, and extend.",
